# Excludes files from the Docker build context. Docker Compose sets the context
# to ./TicketTracker.Api, so every path here is relative to that directory.
#
# This matters because the Dockerfile runs `COPY . ./` - without these rules,
# anything sitting in this folder is copied into an image layer. Layers are
# additive and permanent: deleting a file in a later layer does not remove it
# from the earlier one, and `docker history` recovers it. Same rule as git.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not just noise - obj/project.assets.json is written by the host build and
# holds absolute NuGet paths. On Windows those are C:\Users\... paths, which
# break restore/publish inside a Linux container. Excluding these forces a
# clean restore in the build stage and shrinks the context.
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Oo]ut/
artifacts/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here today: .env lives at the repo root, one level above the build
# context, so Docker cannot reach it. These rules exist so that stays true if
# someone later drops a .env in this folder or widens the context to `.`.
#
# appsettings.json IS copied on purpose - it holds non-secret defaults only.
# MSSQL_PASSWORD and Jwt:Key arrive as environment variables at container
# start, never baked into the image. Keep it that way.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.json
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json

# Certificates and signing material
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.snk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed at build time
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.idea/
*.log
